  "about": "The ids and vocabularies frozen at Stage 0 (ENGINEERING.md §13). The parallel workflows build against these; a change goes through the project manager. Longitudes: a box's bounds are a continuous range written east of 180 where it crosses (pearl-harbor at 201.45–202.45 is 158.55°W–157.55°W); lon0 the same. size is [W, H] in texels, row 0 north, from tools/lib/geo.mjs packGrid over the frozen bounds with the long side at the frozen length; the bake may refine bounds by less than a texel's worth and reports it. metresPerTexel is for reference, in the box's own tangent plane. clock.from/to are the box's clock span (DATA.md §7), with the ISO offset.",
